module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.Completion.AdicQuotientSystem
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.Completion.IdealPowerQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.PrincipalQuotientTowerSections
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.UniformCohomologyBound

/-!
# The two adic towers of a sheaf of modules at a principal ideal agree

Let `X` be a scheme, `ℱ` a sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules and `b ∈ Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` a global function. Two
inverse systems of quotients of `ℱ` are attached to `b`, and this file identifies them and their
inverse limits.

* `Stacks.Algebraization.adicQuotientSystem` at the quasi-coherent ideal sheaf `(b)𝒪_X` is the
  tower `n ↦ ℱ/((b)𝒪_X)ⁿℱ` of quotients by the *subsheaves* cut out by the powers of an ideal
  sheaf, indexed so that level `0` is `ℱ/ℱ = 0`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalQuotientTower.quotientTower` is the tower `n ↦ ℱ/bⁿ⁺¹ℱ` of
  cokernels of the iterates of the *endomorphism* "multiplication by `b`", indexed one step
  later.

They agree level by level, because on an affine open `U` the ideal `((b)𝒪_X)(U)ⁿ` is generated by
`b|_Uⁿ`, so the subsheaf `((b)𝒪_X)ⁿℱ` is the image of `bⁿ : ℱ ⟶ ℱ`; and the one-step index shift
is cofinal, so the two towers have the same inverse limit. Neither statement was in the library:
no file mentioned both constructions.

The levelwise identification is `quotientIso`, the cofinal comparison of the limits is
`ShiftComparison.limitIso`, and its instance at the two towers is `limitTowerIso`. All three come
with their compatibility with the projections out of `ℱ`, which is what a consumer needs and
which also pins the identification down: two quotients of `ℱ` are isomorphic over `ℱ` exactly
when they are quotients by the same subsheaf.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalAdicTower.spanIdealSheaf` — the quasi-coherent ideal sheaf
  `(b)𝒪_X` generated by a global function `b`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalAdicTower.IsMulByTop` — an endomorphism of `ℱ` acts on every
  local section as multiplication by `b`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalAdicTower.quotientIso` — the identification
  `ℱ/((b)𝒪_X)ⁿℱ ≅ ℱ/bⁿℱ` of the two quotients.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.ShiftComparison.IsShiftComparison` and
  `Stacks.Algebraization.ShiftComparison.limitIso` — a one-step comparison of two inverse systems
  indexed by `ℕᵒᵖ`, and the resulting identification of their limits.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalAdicTower.towerComparison` and
  `Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalAdicTower.limitTowerIso` — the comparison of the two towers of
  `ℱ` at a global function, and the identification `lim ℱ/((b)𝒪_X)ⁿℱ ≅ lim ℱ/bⁿ⁺¹ℱ` of their
  limits.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalAdicTower.apply_mem_idealPowerMultiple` and
  `Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalAdicTower.idealPowerMultiple_le_kernelSubmodule` — the two
  inclusions that identify the subsheaf `((b)𝒪_X)ⁿℱ` with the image of `bⁿ`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalAdicTower.π_comp_quotientIso_hom`,
  `.π_comp_quotientIso_inv`, `.limitTowerIso_hom_comp_π` and `.limitTowerIso_inv_comp_π` — the
  compatibility of the comparisons with the projections.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalAdicTower.isMulByTop_mulF` — multiplication by the image of an
  element of a base ring acts by that image on sections, which is what makes
  `Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalQuotientTower.quotientTower` one of the two towers above.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalAdicTower.baseIdealSheaf_span_singleton` — for a principal
  ideal `I = (a)` of the base, `I · 𝒪_X` is the ideal sheaf generated by the image of `a`.

## Implementation notes

The shift by one step is *not* an initial functor on `ℕᵒᵖ`: no level of the shifted system maps
to level `0`. The limits agree all the same, because the level-`0` leg of a cone over the
unshifted system is determined by its level-`1` leg. `ShiftComparison` is that argument, written
out as two cones and two `limit.lift`s rather than through a cofinality statement, which is why
it needs no hypothesis on the index category.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` is a `def` for `SheafOfModules X.ringCatSheaf`, and
`SheafOfModules.Submodule.toSheafOfModules` is declared at the second spelling, so a hom type
built out of it is not one at which instance search finds the zero morphisms of `X.Modules`.
`subSheaf` and `subι` are the submodule and its inclusion with `X.Modules` as the declared type,
which fixes that for every statement here; and the composites that mix the two spellings are
assembled in term mode out of `congrArg` and `Category.assoc`, since a rewrite motive mixing them
is not type-correct at the transparency `rw` builds it at.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0880](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0880)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.InverseSystems.EndIterate (iterate iterate_zero iterate_succ)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower

universe u

attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.submoduleCompleteLattice

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

attribute [local instance] sectionsModuleΓ sectionsModuleΓSheaf sectionsModuleRingCatSheaf
  sectionsSMulCommClassΓ monoSubmoduleι

namespace PrincipalAdicTower

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The module structure on `Γ(M, U)` at the `X.ringCatSheaf` spelling of the ring of sections. -/
local instance sectionsModuleΓPresheaf (M : X.Modules) (U : X.Opens) :
    Module (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U)) Γ(M, U) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Module Γ(X, U) Γ(M, U))

/-- A submodule of a sheaf of modules on `X`, as a sheaf of modules on `X`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` is a `def` for `SheafOfModules X.ringCatSheaf`, and
`SheafOfModules.Submodule.toSheafOfModules` is declared at the latter spelling, so a hom type
built from it is not one at which instance search finds the zero morphisms of `X.Modules`. The
declared result type here is `X.Modules`, which fixes that for every statement below. -/
abbrev subSheaf {F : X.Modules} (N : F.Submodule) : X.Modules := N.toSheafOfModules

/-- The inclusion of a submodule, as a morphism of sheaves of modules on `X`. -/
abbrev subι {F : X.Modules} (N : F.Submodule) : subSheaf N ⟶ F := N.ι

/-- The sectionwise kernel's inclusion, read through the categorical kernel.

Assembled in term mode out of `congrArg` and `Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc`: the composite mixes the
`X.Modules` and `SheafOfModules X.ringCatSheaf` category instances, and a rewrite motive is not
type-correct at the transparency `rw` builds it at. -/
lemma kernelSubmoduleIso_hom_comp_ι {F G : X.Modules} (f : F ⟶ G) :
    (kernelSubmoduleIso f).hom ≫ kernel.ι (C := X.Modules) f = subι (kernelSubmodule f) :=
  (congrArg (fun t ↦ (kernelSubmoduleIso f).hom ≫ t)
      (kernelSubmoduleCorestrict_comp_ι f).symm).trans (Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc _ _)

/-- A composite `u ≫ v` followed by `w` vanishes when `v ≫ w` does. -/
private lemma comp_comp_eq_zero_of_eq {C : Type*} [Category C] [HasZeroMorphisms C]
    {P Q R S : C} {f : P ⟶ R} {u : P ⟶ Q} {v : Q ⟶ R} {w : R ⟶ S}
    (h : f = u ≫ v) (hz : v ≫ w = 0) : f ≫ w = 0 :=
  (congrArg (· ≫ w) h).trans ((Category.assoc _ _ _).trans
    ((congrArg (u ≫ ·) hz).trans comp_zero))

/-- The inclusion of the sectionwise kernel of `f` is killed by `f`. -/
lemma subι_kernelSubmodule_comp {F G : X.Modules} (f : F ⟶ G) :
    subι (kernelSubmodule f) ≫ f = 0 :=
  comp_comp_eq_zero_of_eq (kernelSubmoduleIso_hom_comp_ι f).symm (kernel.condition f)

/-- The restriction to an open `U` of a global function `b` on `X`. -/
abbrev restrictTop (b : Γ(X, ⊤)) (U : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ) : X.presheaf.obj U :=
  (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := U.unop))).op).hom b

/-- On an affine open, the `n`-th power of the quasi-coherent ideal sheaf generated by a global
function `b` is generated by the `n`-th power of the restriction of `b`. -/
lemma pow_ideal_ofIdealTop_span (b : Γ(X, ⊤)) (n : ℕ) (U : X.affineOpens) :
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {b})).ideal U ^ n =
      Ideal.span {restrictTop b (op U.1) ^ n} := by
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton,
    Ideal.span_singleton_pow]

variable {F : X.Modules} {g : F ⟶ F} {b : Γ(X, ⊤)}

/-- The ideal sheaf generated by a global function, the one whose powers cut out the tower
compared below. -/
abbrev spanIdealSheaf (b : Γ(X, ⊤)) : X.IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {b})

/-- `g` acts on sections as multiplication by the global function `b`. -/
abbrev IsMulByTop (g : F ⟶ F) (b : Γ(X, ⊤)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (U : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ) (x : F.val.obj U), (g.val.app U).hom x = restrictTop b U • x

/-- The iterates of an endomorphism acting as multiplication by `b` act by the powers of `b`. -/
lemma iterate_val_app (hg : IsMulByTop g b) (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ) (x : F.val.obj U) :
    ((iterate g n).val.app U).hom x = restrictTop b U ^ n • x := by
  induction n generalizing x with
  | zero =>
      have h1 : ((iterate g 0).val.app U).hom x = x := rfl
      rw [h1, pow_zero]
      exact (one_smul _ x).symm
  | succ k ih =>
      have hcomp : ((iterate g (k + 1)).val.app U).hom x =
          ((iterate g k).val.app U).hom ((g.val.app U).hom x) := rfl
      rw [hcomp, hg U x, ih, smul_smul]
      exact congrArg (fun r : X.presheaf.obj U ↦ r • x) (pow_succ (restrictTop b U) k).symm

/-- A section in the image of `g ^ n` lies in the subsheaf `𝓘 ^ n F`: affine-locally the image
of `g ^ n` is `b ^ n • Γ(F, U)`, one of the generators of `𝓘 ^ n F`. -/
lemma apply_mem_idealPowerMultiple (hg : IsMulByTop g b) (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : F.val.obj U) :
    ((iterate g n).val.app U).hom x ∈
      (idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F).toSubmodule.obj U := by
  refine mem_submodule_of_affine _ U.unop _ fun V i ↦ ?_
  have hmem : restrictTop b (op V.1) ^ n •
      (show F.val.obj (op V.1) from (F.val.map i.op).hom x) ∈
        (idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F).toSubmodule.obj (op V.1) := by
    refine le_idealPowerMultiple_obj _ n F V (Submodule.smul_mem_smul ?_ Submodule.mem_top)
    rw [pow_ideal_ofIdealTop_span b n V]
    exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _
  have hnat : (show F.val.obj (op V.1) from
        (F.val.map i.op).hom (((iterate g n).val.app U).hom x)) =
      restrictTop b (op V.1) ^ n • (show F.val.obj (op V.1) from (F.val.map i.op).hom x) :=
    (congrArg (fun k ↦ k x)
        (PresheafOfModules.Hom.naturality (iterate g n).val i.op)).symm.trans
      (iterate_val_app hg n (op V.1) _)
  exact Eq.mpr (congrArg
    (· ∈ (idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F).toSubmodule.obj (op V.1)) hnat) hmem

/-- The subsheaf `𝓘 ^ n F` lies in the sectionwise kernel of the cokernel projection of `g ^ n`:
affine-locally it is generated by the sections `b ^ n • m`, and those are in the image of
`g ^ n`. -/
lemma idealPowerMultiple_le_kernelSubmodule (hg : IsMulByTop g b) (n : ℕ) :
    idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F ≤
      kernelSubmodule (cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (iterate g n)) := by
  refine (idealPowerMultiple_le_iff _ n F _).2 fun U ↦ ?_
  refine Submodule.smul_le.mpr fun r hr m _ ↦ ?_
  rw [pow_ideal_ofIdealTop_span b n U] at hr
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 hr
  have key : (show F.val.obj (op U.1) from r • m) =
      c • ((iterate g n).val.app (op U.1)).hom (show F.val.obj (op U.1) from m) :=
    (congrArg (fun s : X.presheaf.obj (op U.1) ↦ s • (show F.val.obj (op U.1) from m))
        hc.symm).trans
      ((mul_smul c (restrictTop b (op U.1) ^ n) (show F.val.obj (op U.1) from m)).trans
        (congrArg (fun y ↦ c • y) (iterate_val_app hg n (op U.1) _).symm))
  have hz : ((cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (iterate g n)).val.app (op U.1)).hom
      (((iterate g n).val.app (op U.1)).hom (show F.val.obj (op U.1) from m)) = 0 :=
    congrArg (fun k : F ⟶ cokernel (C := X.Modules) (iterate g n) ↦
        (k.val.app (op U.1)).hom (show F.val.obj (op U.1) from m))
      (cokernel.condition (C := X.Modules) (iterate g n))
  refine Eq.mpr (congrArg
    (· ∈ (kernelSubmodule (cokernel.π (C := X.Modules)
      (iterate g n))).toSubmodule.obj (op U.1)) key) ?_
  rw [kernelSubmodule_toSubmodule_obj]
  refine LinearMap.mem_ker.2 ?_
  rw [map_smul, hz, smul_zero]

/-- The corestriction of `g ^ n` to the subsheaf `𝓘 ^ n F`, which contains its image. -/
def iterateLift (hg : IsMulByTop g b) (n : ℕ) :
    F ⟶ subSheaf (idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F) :=
  (AlgebraicGeometry.sheafTopIso F).inv ≫
    AlgebraicGeometry.sheafSubmoduleMap (iterate g n) ⊤
      (idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F)
      (SheafOfModules.Submodule.le_iff.2 fun U x _ ↦ apply_mem_idealPowerMultiple hg n U x)

/-- The corestriction of `g ^ n` to `𝓘 ^ n F`, followed by the inclusion, is `g ^ n`. -/
lemma iterateLift_comp_ι (hg : IsMulByTop g b) (n : ℕ) :
    iterateLift hg n ≫ subι (idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F) = iterate g n :=
  (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans
    ((congrArg (fun k ↦ (AlgebraicGeometry.sheafTopIso F).inv ≫ k)
        (AlgebraicGeometry.sheafSubmoduleMap_comp_ι _ _ _ _)).trans
      ((Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
        ((congrArg (fun k ↦ k ≫ iterate g n)
            (AlgebraicGeometry.sheafTopIso F).inv_hom_id).trans (Category.id_comp _))))

/-- The inclusion of `𝓘 ^ n F` into `F` is killed by the cokernel projection of `g ^ n`. -/
lemma subι_comp_cokernelπ (hg : IsMulByTop g b) (n : ℕ) :
    subι (idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F) ≫
      cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (iterate g n) = 0 :=
  comp_comp_eq_zero_of_eq
    (submoduleInclusion_comp_ι (idealPowerMultiple_le_kernelSubmodule hg n)).symm
    (subι_kernelSubmodule_comp _)

/-- `g ^ n` is killed by the projection onto the quotient of `F` by `𝓘 ^ n F`. -/
lemma iterate_comp_cokernelπ (hg : IsMulByTop g b) (n : ℕ) :
    iterate g n ≫
        cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (subι (idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F)) = 0 :=
  comp_comp_eq_zero_of_eq (iterateLift_comp_ι hg n).symm (cokernel.condition _)

/-- **The two quotients agree.** For `𝓘` the ideal sheaf generated by a global function `b` and
`g` multiplication by `b`, the quotient of `F` by the subsheaf `𝓘 ^ n F` is the cokernel of
`g ^ n`, compatibly with the two projections out of `F`. -/
def quotientIso (hg : IsMulByTop g b) (n : ℕ) :
    cokernel (C := X.Modules) (subι (idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F)) ≅
      cokernel (C := X.Modules) (iterate g n) where
  hom := cokernel.desc (C := X.Modules) _ (cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (iterate g n))
    (subι_comp_cokernelπ hg n)
  inv := cokernel.desc (C := X.Modules) _
    (cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (subι (idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F)))
    (iterate_comp_cokernelπ hg n)
  hom_inv_id := by
    refine coequalizer.hom_ext ?_
    rw [← Category.assoc, cokernel.π_desc, cokernel.π_desc, Category.comp_id]
  inv_hom_id := by
    refine coequalizer.hom_ext ?_
    rw [← Category.assoc, cokernel.π_desc, cokernel.π_desc, Category.comp_id]

/-- The comparison of quotients is compatible with the projections out of `F`. -/
lemma π_comp_quotientIso_hom (hg : IsMulByTop g b) (n : ℕ) :
    cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (subι (idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F)) ≫
        (quotientIso hg n).hom = cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (iterate g n) :=
  cokernel.π_desc _ _ _

/-- The inverse comparison of quotients is compatible with the projections out of `F`. -/
lemma π_comp_quotientIso_inv (hg : IsMulByTop g b) (n : ℕ) :
    cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (iterate g n) ≫ (quotientIso hg n).inv =
      cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (subι (idealPowerMultiple (spanIdealSheaf b) n F)) :=
  cokernel.π_desc _ _ _

end PrincipalAdicTower

/-! ### Reindexing an inverse system by one step does not change its limit -/

namespace ShiftComparison

variable {C : Type*} [Category C] (D E : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ C) [HasLimit D] [HasLimit E]
  (κ : ∀ n : ℕ, E.obj (op n) ≅ D.obj (op (n + 1)))

/-- The compatibility of a one-step comparison with the transition maps of the two systems. -/
abbrev IsShiftComparison : Prop :=
  ∀ n : ℕ, (κ (n + 1)).hom ≫ D.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ (n + 1))).op =
    E.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)).op ≫ (κ n).hom

omit [HasLimit D] [HasLimit E] in
/-- The compatibility, read for the inverse of the comparison. -/
lemma isShiftComparison_inv (hκ : IsShiftComparison D E κ) (n : ℕ) :
    D.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ (n + 1))).op ≫ (κ n).inv =
      (κ (n + 1)).inv ≫ E.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)).op := by
  rw [Iso.eq_inv_comp, ← Category.assoc, hκ n, Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id,
    Category.comp_id]

omit [HasLimit D] in
/-- The naturality of the legs of `coneOfShifted`. -/
lemma coneOfShifted_naturality (hκ : IsShiftComparison D E κ) (n : ℕ) :
    limit.π E (op n) ≫ (κ n).hom ≫ D.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)).op =
      (limit.π E (op (n + 1)) ≫ (κ (n + 1)).hom ≫
        D.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ (n + 1))).op) ≫ D.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)).op := by
  rw [← limit.w E (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)).op]
  simp only [Category.assoc, reassoc_of% hκ n]

omit [HasLimit E] in
/-- The naturality of the legs of `coneOfUnshifted`. -/
lemma coneOfUnshifted_naturality (hκ : IsShiftComparison D E κ) (n : ℕ) :
    limit.π D (op (n + 1)) ≫ (κ n).inv =
      (limit.π D (op (n + 1 + 1)) ≫ (κ (n + 1)).inv) ≫
        E.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)).op := by
  rw [← limit.w D (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ (n + 1))).op]
  simp only [Category.assoc, isShiftComparison_inv D E κ hκ n]

/-- The comparison from the limit of `D` to the limit of the shifted system. -/
def shiftHom (hκ : IsShiftComparison D E κ) : limit D ⟶ limit E :=
  limit.lift E
    { pt := limit D
      π := NatTrans.ofOpSequence
        (fun n ↦ limit.π D (op (n + 1)) ≫ (κ n).inv)
        (fun n ↦ (Category.id_comp _).trans (coneOfUnshifted_naturality D E κ hκ n)) }

/-- The comparison from the limit of the shifted system to the limit of `D`: the level-`m` leg
is the level-`m` projection of `E`, carried to level `m + 1` of `D` and pushed down one step. -/
def shiftInv (hκ : IsShiftComparison D E κ) : limit E ⟶ limit D :=
  limit.lift D
    { pt := limit E
      π := NatTrans.ofOpSequence
        (fun n ↦ limit.π E (op n) ≫ (κ n).hom ≫ D.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)).op)
        (fun n ↦ (Category.id_comp _).trans (coneOfShifted_naturality D E κ hκ n)) }

/-- The comparison is compatible with the projections of the shifted system. -/
lemma shiftHom_comp_π (hκ : IsShiftComparison D E κ) (n : ℕ) :
    shiftHom D E κ hκ ≫ limit.π E (op n) = limit.π D (op (n + 1)) ≫ (κ n).inv :=
  limit.lift_π _ _

/-- The inverse comparison is compatible with the projections of `D`. -/
lemma shiftInv_comp_π (hκ : IsShiftComparison D E κ) (m : ℕ) :
    shiftInv D E κ hκ ≫ limit.π D (op m) =
      limit.π E (op m) ≫ (κ m).hom ≫ D.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ m)).op :=
  limit.lift_π _ _

/-- **Shifting an inverse system by one step does not change its limit.** -/
def limitIso (hκ : IsShiftComparison D E κ) : limit D ≅ limit E where
  hom := shiftHom D E κ hκ
  inv := shiftInv D E κ hκ
  hom_inv_id := by
    refine limit.hom_ext fun j ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨m⟩ := j
    rw [Category.id_comp, Category.assoc, shiftInv_comp_π D E κ hκ m, ← Category.assoc,
      shiftHom_comp_π D E κ hκ m]
    simp only [Category.assoc]
    rw [Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc, limit.w D (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ m)).op]
  inv_hom_id := by
    refine limit.hom_ext fun j ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨n⟩ := j
    rw [Category.id_comp, Category.assoc, shiftHom_comp_π D E κ hκ n, ← Category.assoc,
      shiftInv_comp_π D E κ hκ (n + 1)]
    simp only [Category.assoc]
    rw [isShiftComparison_inv D E κ hκ n, Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc,
      limit.w E (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)).op]

end ShiftComparison

/-! ### The two towers of a coherent sheaf at a principal ideal -/

namespace PrincipalAdicTower

open Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedSectionsOverBase (baseSmul)
open Stacks.Algebraization.PrincipalQuotientTower (mulF quotientTower quotientTowerModules
  quotientTower_map_succ)

variable (X : Scheme.{u}) {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (ρ : A →+* Γ(X, ⊤)) (a : A) (ℱ : X.Modules)

/-- Multiplication by the image of `a` in `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` acts on sections by that image. -/
lemma isMulByTop_mulF : IsMulByTop (mulF X ρ a ℱ) (ρ a) := fun U x ↦
  (Stacks.SheafOfModules.terminalSectionToEnd_apply (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) ⊤
      isTerminalTop (ρ a) ℱ U x).trans
    (congrArg
      (fun k : U.unop ⟶ (⊤ : Opens X.toRingedSpace.carrier) ↦
        (X.presheaf.map k.op).hom (ρ a) • x)
      (Subsingleton.elim (isTerminalTop.from U.unop) (homOfLE (le_top (a := U.unop)))))

/-- The projections out of `ℱ` are compatible with the transitions of the adic quotient tower. -/
lemma π_comp_adicQuotientSystem_map (I : X.IdealSheafData) {i j : ℕ} (h : j ≤ i) :
    cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (subι (idealPowerMultiple I i ℱ)) ≫
        (adicQuotientSystem I ℱ).map (homOfLE h).op =
      cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (subι (idealPowerMultiple I j ℱ)) :=
  quotientMapOfLE_π (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerMultiple_antitone I ℱ h)

/-- The projections out of `ℱ` are compatible with the transitions of the quotient tower. -/
lemma π_comp_quotientTower_map (n : ℕ) :
    cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (iterate (mulF X ρ a ℱ) (n + 1 + 1)) ≫
        (quotientTowerModules X ρ a ℱ).map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)).op =
      cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (iterate (mulF X ρ a ℱ) (n + 1)) := by
  rw [quotientTower_map_succ X ρ a ℱ n]
  exact (cokernel.π_desc _ _ _).trans (Category.id_comp _)

/-- **The comparison of the two towers, level by level.** Level `n` of the quotient tower of `ℱ`
at `a` is level `n + 1` of the adic quotient tower of `ℱ` at the ideal sheaf `(a)𝒪_X`. -/
def towerComparison (n : ℕ) :
    (quotientTowerModules X ρ a ℱ).obj (op n) ≅
      (adicQuotientSystem (spanIdealSheaf (ρ a)) ℱ).obj (op (n + 1)) :=
  (quotientIso (isMulByTop_mulF X ρ a ℱ) (n + 1)).symm

/-- The comparison of towers is compatible with the transition maps: a one-step comparison in
the sense of `ShiftComparison.IsShiftComparison`. -/
lemma isShiftComparison_towerComparison :
    ShiftComparison.IsShiftComparison (adicQuotientSystem (spanIdealSheaf (ρ a)) ℱ)
      (quotientTowerModules X ρ a ℱ) (towerComparison X ρ a ℱ) := fun n ↦
  (cancel_epi (cokernel.π (C := X.Modules) (iterate (mulF X ρ a ℱ) (n + 1 + 1)))).1
    (((Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
        ((congrArg (fun t ↦ t ≫ (adicQuotientSystem (spanIdealSheaf (ρ a)) ℱ).map
                (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ (n + 1))).op)
            (π_comp_quotientIso_inv (isMulByTop_mulF X ρ a ℱ) (n + 1 + 1))).trans
          (π_comp_adicQuotientSystem_map X ℱ (spanIdealSheaf (ρ a))
            (Nat.le_succ (n + 1))))).trans
      ((Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
        ((congrArg (fun t ↦ t ≫ (towerComparison X ρ a ℱ n).hom)
            (π_comp_quotientTower_map X ρ a ℱ n)).trans
          (π_comp_quotientIso_inv (isMulByTop_mulF X ρ a ℱ) (n + 1)))).symm)

/-- **The formal completion of `ℱ` at a principal ideal, computed on either tower.** The inverse
limit of the adic quotient tower `n ↦ ℱ/((a)𝒪_X)ⁿℱ` is the inverse limit of the quotient tower
`n ↦ ℱ/aⁿ⁺¹ℱ`; the one-step index shift is absorbed by the comparison. -/
def limitTowerIso :
    limit (adicQuotientSystem (spanIdealSheaf (ρ a)) ℱ) ≅ limit (quotientTowerModules X ρ a ℱ) :=
  ShiftComparison.limitIso _ _ (towerComparison X ρ a ℱ)
    (isShiftComparison_towerComparison X ρ a ℱ)

/-- The comparison of limits is compatible with the projections of the quotient tower. -/
lemma limitTowerIso_hom_comp_π (n : ℕ) :
    (limitTowerIso X ρ a ℱ).hom ≫ limit.π (quotientTowerModules X ρ a ℱ) (op n) =
      limit.π (adicQuotientSystem (spanIdealSheaf (ρ a)) ℱ) (op (n + 1)) ≫
        (towerComparison X ρ a ℱ n).inv :=
  ShiftComparison.shiftHom_comp_π _ _ _ (isShiftComparison_towerComparison X ρ a ℱ) n

/-- The comparison of limits is compatible with the projections of the adic quotient tower. -/
lemma limitTowerIso_inv_comp_π (m : ℕ) :
    (limitTowerIso X ρ a ℱ).inv ≫
        limit.π (adicQuotientSystem (spanIdealSheaf (ρ a)) ℱ) (op m) =
      limit.π (quotientTowerModules X ρ a ℱ) (op m) ≫ (towerComparison X ρ a ℱ m).hom ≫
        (adicQuotientSystem (spanIdealSheaf (ρ a)) ℱ).map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ m)).op :=
  ShiftComparison.shiftInv_comp_π _ _ _ (isShiftComparison_towerComparison X ρ a ℱ) m

/-- The ideal sheaf `I · 𝒪_X` of a principal ideal `I = (a)` of the base is the ideal sheaf
generated by the image of `a` in `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`. -/
lemma baseIdealSheaf_span_singleton {Y : Scheme.{u}} (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (f : Y ⟶ Spec (.of A)) (a : A) :
    Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf A (Ideal.span {a}) f =
      spanIdealSheaf (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv ≫ f.appTop).hom a) :=
  congrArg Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
    (by rw [Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdeal, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton])

end PrincipalAdicTower

end Stacks.Algebraization

